An interface one function takes as a parameter type, with one implementation, and a
method the function calls through the interface. A satisfaction assertion names the
interface as well, so the assertion is not the only thing that does.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27.0
-- main.go --
package main

// Reader reads a line.
type Reader interface {
	Read() string
}

type file struct{}

func (file) Read() string { return "ok" }

var _ Reader = file{}

func first(r Reader) string { return r.Read() }

func main() { println(first(file{})) }
